WEBVTT

00:00:00.455 --> 00:00:05.930
Your business holds Bitcoin but needs working capital With Tillward you borrow

00:00:05.955 --> 00:00:09.394
against that Bitcoin and repay from customer receipts

00:00:10.455 --> 00:00:16.246
Borrow MUSD against Bitcoin through Mezo Check the native price collateral ratios

00:00:16.271 --> 00:00:19.776
and Recovery Mode Add collateral when you choose

00:00:25.442 --> 00:00:30.496
Choose your repayment share up to ninety-nine percent Enable automation when you're

00:00:30.521 --> 00:00:35.158
ready Tillward charges one percent of the amount actually repaid

00:00:39.442 --> 00:00:43.614
Create an invoice and share the payment link Your customer approves the

00:00:43.639 --> 00:00:49.285
exact MUSD amount then pays The receipt and its repayment allocation are

00:00:49.311 --> 00:00:51.290
recorded in your business account

00:00:54.455 --> 00:01:00.259
At twenty percent a five-hundred MUSD payment repays one hundred The service

00:01:00.284 --> 00:01:05.316
fee is one MUSD Three hundred ninety-nine stays with the business

00:01:09.455 --> 00:01:14.575
The public test used the ninety-nine percent cap Five hundred MUSD came

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:19.329
in four hundred ninety-five repaid four point nine five paid the fee

00:01:19.482 --> 00:01:23.566
and zero point zero five remained In one transaction

00:01:26.442 --> 00:01:30.891
You can pause automation and still manage your loan We verified manual

00:01:30.916 --> 00:01:35.391
repayment without another service fee then closure and the return of zero

00:01:35.416 --> 00:01:37.737
point zero four five test Bitcoin

00:01:41.455 --> 00:01:46.575
We also created real redemption surplus claimed it through Tillward and withdrew

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:50.838
the Bitcoin The public receipts and exact balance checks are linked in

00:01:50.863 --> 00:01:52.000
the judge guide

00:01:54.442 --> 00:01:59.145
Try Tillward Follow the receipts and explore the code on GitHub
